# schedule behavior in xpcom/rust/moz_task/src/executor.rs

Checks thread-local identity to set or clear AT_END. Enables fallible dispatch when running on the chosen event target. Captures a config clone and runnable in a closure that saves current polling identity, sets this task identity, runs the runnable, then restores the previous identity. Selects background or explicit target dispatch and logs an error.

## State read

- POLLING_TASK raw config pointer; config target/options/name/priority; target thread predicate

## State changed

- options AT_END/FALLIBLE flags; POLLING_TASK temporarily replaced around run

## Calls and triggers

- is_on_current_thread to native predicate; RunnableBuilder::new/priority/options; dispatcher dispatch_background_task or dispatch; async_task::Runnable::run.

## Result and consumers

Unit. Dispatch failures are logged rather than returned to AsyncTask consumer.

## Errors

The restoration uses straight-line code, so a panic from runnable.run that unwinds through this closure skips t.set(prev); runtime panic policy/dependency catching is unresolved. Failed dispatch uses target/flag-specific release behavior.

## Async completion

This is the scheduler callback from async_task spawn. Wakes while currently polling the same config get AT_END; cancellation semantics depend on runnable drop and wrapper poll mapping.

## Ownership and cleanup

Arc config is cloned into queued closure and retained while runnable lives; explicit target is retained by config RefPtr. Callback consumes runnable.

